140	   139	/**
141	   140	 * Completes card setup after Stripe redirects back to
142	   141	 * `/dashboard/billing?card_setup=<session_id>`.
143	   142	 *
144	   143	 * Two things this must not be:
145	   144	 *  - a silent no-op. Checkout attaches the card at Stripe BEFORE this ever runs,
146	   145	 *    so a customer who lands here and sees nothing has a card at Stripe and none
147	   146	 *    on file with us — and would be dunned for it.
148	   147	 *  - a dead end. If finalising fails, the card may still be saved at Stripe, and
149	   148	 *    the worker's `adoptUnclaimedCards` backstop claims it on the next sweep. The
150	   149	 *    failure copy says exactly that, and still offers a retry.
151	   150	 *
152	   151	 * `finalizeCardSetup` is documented as safe to call repeatedly with the same
153	   152	 * session id, so a refreshed tab re-reads the same payment method rather than
154	   153	 * saving a second card. The ref below is not for correctness, only to stop React's
155	   154	 * development double-mount from firing two identical round-trips.
156	   155	 */
